<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33657" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παννονία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a country lying
				between Dacia</i>, <i>Noricum</i>, <i>and Illyria</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 25,
				28, § 147</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 2,
				225</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnĭăcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Pannonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">augures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Sev. 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Pannonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cattae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 69, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannonicae stirpis canes, Nemes, Cyn. 126:
					pilei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 1, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			adj., <i>Pannonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannonis ursa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 220</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Pannonian; subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pannŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a
			Pannonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fallax Pannonius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					4, 1, 109</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 4, 78</span></i>
			.—More freq. plur., <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1,
				4, 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. I. Cons. Stil. 2,
				191</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
